@startuml state-diagram
title CampusConnect - GoF State Pattern: Course Enrollment Lifecycle

[*] --> DRAFT : Student creates enrollment draft\n[new Enrollment()]

state DRAFT {
    DRAFT : Initial creation state
    DRAFT : Modifiable by student
}

DRAFT --> SUBMITTED : submit()\n[Student submits application]

state SUBMITTED {
    SUBMITTED : Application locked
    SUBMITTED : Under Academic Administrator review
}

SUBMITTED --> APPROVED : approve()\n[Admin approves prerequisites & capacity]
SUBMITTED --> REJECTED : reject()\n[Admin rejects application]

state APPROVED {
    APPROVED : Awaiting semester commencement
    APPROVED : Seat reserved in course capacity
}

APPROVED --> ENROLLED : finalizeEnrollment()\n[Admin / Registrar confirms roster]
APPROVED --> REJECTED : reject()\n[Admin cancels approval]

state ENROLLED {
    ENROLLED : Active participant in class meetings
    ENROLLED : Attendance tracked
    ENROLLED : Coursework evaluated & graded
}

ENROLLED --> DROPPED : drop()\n[Student or Admin drops before deadline]

state DROPPED {
    DROPPED : Course dropped
    DROPPED : Seat released back to course capacity
}

state REJECTED {
    REJECTED : Application denied
    REJECTED : Terminal state
}

DROPPED --> [*]
REJECTED --> [*]

note right of DRAFT
    <b>Encapsulated Invariant</b>:
    State transitions are delegated to
    polymorphic EnrollmentState implementations.
    Direct illegal transitions throw IllegalStateException.
end note

@enduml
